# MiniMax-M2 (MiniMax, 2025): an MoE of 230B parameters, 10B of them active a token,
# for coding and agentic work, with a context of 196,608 tokens. All 62 layers are full
# attention, 48 query heads over 8 key and value heads of 128, the queries twice the
# width. QK-norm normalizes all the query heads together, and all the key heads, before
# RoPE turns the first half of each head's dims. Every FFN is an MoE of 256 experts,
# none shared. A token goes to the 8 whose sigmoid scores are best once a bias that
# balances the experts' loads is added, weighted by their scores over the 8's sum.
#
# The config lists three multi-token prediction modules, but the checkpoint has no
# weights for them and no published code describes them: they are not described here.
d_model    = 3072
vocab_size = 200064

norm    = rmsnorm(eps=1e-6)
attn    = gqa(num_heads=48, num_kv_heads=8, head_dim=128, qk_norm=norm,
              qk_norm_all_heads=true, rope=rope(base=5000000, fraction=0.5))
experts = moe(num_experts=256, top_k=8, router=sigmoid, load_balancing=aux_free,
              aux_loss_coef=1e-3, expert=gated_mlp(intermediate_size=1536, activation=swish))

block = [norm attn] [norm experts]
model = embed block^62 norm head
